---
import KCLayout from "../../layouts/KCLayout.astro";
---

<KCLayout
    title="About this directory — KC"
    description="Who runs the Kansas City directory, how listings are built, and how corrections are handled."
>
    <p class="kc-eyebrow">About this directory</p>
    <h1>Who runs this and how it works.</h1>
    <p class="kc-lede">
        This directory is run by CivicBrands — a small civic-infrastructure operation in Kansas City.
        People use this directory to make real decisions about where to call and where to go. We
        want to be clear about who we are, how listings are built, and what we cannot promise.
    </p>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="who">
        <h2 id="who">Who</h2>
        <p>
            CivicBrands is the DBA of BJL13 Enterprise Solutions LLC, a Missouri company. The site is
            written and maintained by CivicBrands and a rotating set of community contributors.
            It is not a city government project, not a funded nonprofit program, and not a venture-
            backed startup. It does not run on ads. It does not sell data. It exists because the
            metro needs a directory like this and because no single agency was going to build one
            that crosses the state line.
        </p>
        <p>
            Reach CivicBrands directly: <a href="mailto:corrections@mail.civicbrands.org">corrections@mail.civicbrands.org</a>
            · <a href="tel:+18163063481">816-306-3481</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="listing-build">
        <h2 id="listing-build">How listings are built</h2>
        <p>
            We call, visit, read public material, and listen to people who have used the service.
            That work stays behind the page. On the page, we write the part that helps someone
            decide whether to call, go, or keep looking.
        </p>
        <p>
            Programs change without notice. Hours move. Numbers disconnect. Funding ends. Always
            call ahead when you can.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="how-submit">
        <h2 id="how-submit">How submissions are reviewed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Every submission goes into a private queue we review by hand.</li>
            <li>Urgent reports — a critical number stopped working, a service is turning people away — are reviewed within 24 hours.</li>
            <li>New service suggestions are typically reviewed within a week, often faster.</li>
            <li>If we add an entry, we include what a person needs to decide whether to call, go, or keep looking.</li>
            <li>We do not publish your name or contact info on the public site without your explicit permission.</li>
            <li>We may follow up with a question, only if you provided contact info.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="cannot">
        <h2 id="cannot">What we cannot promise</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>That any specific service is open right now. Hours change.</li>
            <li>That a service will accept you when you arrive. Eligibility decisions are made by the service, not by us.</li>
            <li>That we will catch every change as it happens. We need your help — flag anything wrong.</li>
            <li>That a service is high-quality. We can tell you a service exists and operates; we cannot vouch for the experience of any particular interaction.</li>
            <li>Legal or medical advice. Nothing here is legal or medical advice. We list services; we do not provide them.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="not-shared">
        <h2 id="not-shared">What is not shared</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>We do not sell or share submissions with anyone, including the services they reference.</li>
            <li>We do not share IP addresses or browser fingerprints beyond what Cloudflare requires for the request to function.</li>
            <li>We do not use third-party analytics or trackers on this site. No Google Analytics, no Meta Pixel, no Hotjar, no cookies for tracking. See our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for the longer version.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="mirror">
        <h2 id="mirror">Free to mirror</h2>
        <p>
            The directory data is free to mirror, redistribute, repost. Use the machine-readable exports
            at <a href="/kc/services.json">services.json</a> and <a href="/kc/services.csv">services.csv</a>.
            Crisis numbers are at <a href="/kc/crisis.txt">crisis.txt</a> and <a href="/kc/crisis.json">crisis.json</a>.
            Attribution is welcome but not required. If you find an error in a mirrored copy, please
            also let us know so the upstream gets corrected.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="conflict">
        <h2 id="conflict">If something here harmed you</h2>
        <p>
            If you went to a service we listed and were harmed — turned away, treated badly, surveilled,
            denied, or worse — please tell us. We need to know so we can correct the guidance, add
            context, or remove the listing.
        </p>
        <p>
            <a href="mailto:corrections@mail.civicbrands.org">corrections@mail.civicbrands.org</a>. Use <a href="/kc/suggest">the suggest form</a>
            if you would rather not email.
        </p>
    </section>
</KCLayout>
